---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { u, MAILING_ADDRESS } from '../../lib/site.js';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="What The Celtic Coo collects, why, and the choices you have.">
  <div style="max-width:760px">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Effective October 26, 2026</p>
    <p>The Celtic Coo (CelticCoo.ca) is a small, independent guide to Highland Games, pipe bands, Highland dance and Celtic events across Canada, run from Alberta, Canada. This page explains in plain language what information we collect, why we collect it, and the choices you have.</p>
    <p><b>The short version:</b> you can use CelticCoo.ca without giving us any personal information. We don't set our own cookies, we don't use advertising trackers, and we never sell your personal information.</p>

    <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
    <p>"The Celtic Coo", "we" and "us" mean the operator of this website, based in Alberta, Canada.</p>

    <h2 id="visits">When you visit the site</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Analytics.</b> We don't run analytics scripts. Cloudflare gives us basic totals, like visits per day, from its own server records.</li>
      <li><b>Hosting.</b> The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare handles your IP address and basic request details to deliver pages and protect the site from attacks. If it needs to check that you're not a bot, Cloudflare may set a short-lived security cookie. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Your tartan banner.</b> If you pick a tartan for the page banner on <a href={u('tartans/')}>Find your tartan</a>, your choice is saved only in your own browser (local storage). It's never sent to us. Use the reset button on that page, or clear your browser's site data, to remove it.</li>
      <li><b>Your display settings.</b> If you change text size, contrast or font in the accessibility menu, that choice is saved only in your browser. It's never sent to us.</li>
      <li><b>Calendar and RSS feeds.</b> Subscribing to our calendar or RSS feed doesn't ask for any personal information.</li>
      <li><b>No accounts.</b> There are no logins, comments or user profiles.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="newsletter">The Coo's Letter (newsletter)</h2>
    <p>Our email, sent every two weeks, runs on <a href="https://kit.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Kit</a> (formerly ConvertKit). The sign-up form asks for your <b>email address</b> and nothing else. Kit stores your address, when you signed up, and standard email statistics such as opens and clicks. We'll use your address only to send The Coo's Letter.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>We only email you if you've signed up yourself, as Canada's Anti-Spam Legislation (CASL) requires.</li>
      <li>Every email says who it's from and has an unsubscribe link.</li>
      <li>You can unsubscribe at any time with one click, and we'll stop emailing you right away.</li>
      <li>Every newsletter shows our name, mailing address and a one-click unsubscribe link. We act on an unsubscribe right away, and always within 10 business days.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="booking">When you ask us to find a performer</h2>
    <p>The <a href={u('book/')}>Book performers</a> page is for people who want an introduction to an independent piper, drummer, band, Highland dancer, heavy athlete or other Celtic performer. The form asks for your name, email, an optional phone number, the kind of request, the event (or your own event's type, name, date, city and province), the performer types you need, a message, and an optional budget range. You also tell us whether the performer or competitor is under 18.</p>
    <p>The <a href={u('book/checklist/')}>booking details checklist</a> is a worksheet you can print and keep. It is not sent to us, and it is not a contract.</p>
    <p>We keep that request in a private database so we can check it, reply, and follow up, and we email a notice to a private inbox we control. We do not put the request on the website, and we do not store it in the public site files. We do not publish your name, email or phone. We share contact details with a performer only after both sides agree. We never publish the name of anyone under 18, and the form does not ask for a minor's name. If we write back, the reply comes from <a href="mailto:bookings@celticcoo.ca">bookings@celticcoo.ca</a> or <a href="mailto:hello@celticcoo.ca">hello@celticcoo.ca</a>, and a person sends it. The form also asks you to confirm you are a person. That check is done by Cloudflare and is not used to build a profile of you.</p>
    <p>The form has a consent checkbox. We only email you about the request if you tick it, which is what Canada's anti-spam law (CASL) asks for. You can tell us to stop at any time.</p>

    <h2 id="submissions">When you send us an event, shop or correction</h2>
    <p>Our <a href={u('submit/')}>Add yours</a> page lets you send us an event, a shop listing or a correction by email. We use what you send to check and publish the listing. We publish the event or business details, such as the name, dates, location and website. We don't publish your personal name or email address unless you ask us to. We keep your email so we can follow up about the listing. If we add an online submission form later, the same rules will apply.</p>

    <h2 id="email">When you email us</h2>
    <p>When you email <a href="mailto:hello@celticcoo.ca">hello@celticcoo.ca</a>, a copy goes to a private inbox we control. We also keep the sender, subject and text in a private database so nothing gets lost. Attachments aren't stored.</p>
    <p>An automated tool run by Cloudflare sorts each email, for example event, correction or booking. It doesn't make decisions about you.</p>
    <p>If you send an event or a correction, we may open a task to check it. That task only holds the public event details, like the name, date, place and website. It never holds your name, email, phone or message.</p>
    <p>If we need more details, we may write back. A person reads and approves every reply before it's sent.</p>

    <h2 id="affiliates">Affiliate links and retailer cookies</h2>
    <p>The Celtic Coo doesn't have any affiliate links right now. Links to shops, organizers and associations are ordinary links. If we add affiliate partners in the future, those links will be clearly labelled, and we may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you.</p>
    <p>When you click an affiliate link, the retailer or its affiliate network may set cookies <b>on its own site</b> so it knows you came from us. We don't set those cookies, and the retailer's own privacy policy covers them. We'd only get summary reports, such as how many clicks and sales a link produced. We'd never see your name, address or payment details. You can block or clear these cookies in your browser settings.</p>

    <h2 id="sharing">We don't sell your information</h2>
    <p>We never sell, rent or trade personal information. We use a few services to run the site, and they only handle it for us:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Cloudflare:</b> hosting, security and the "confirm you are a person" check, the private database for requests and emails, sending and forwarding email, the automated email sorting, and (soon) image storage.</li>
      <li><b>Kit:</b> The Coo's Letter newsletter.</li>
      <li><b>GitHub:</b> where the site's code and our listing to-do list live. No personal details go there.</li>
      <li><b>Our email provider:</b> the private inbox that receives booking notices and email copies.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We share contact details with a performer only after both of you agree, or when the law requires it.</p>

    <h2 id="storage">Where it's stored and for how long</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare and Kit are based in the United States, so your information may be stored or processed outside Canada and may be subject to the laws there.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Booking requests: 12 months after we last reply, then deleted.</li>
      <li>Emails to hello@: 12 months, then deleted.</li>
      <li>Failed or spam form attempts: a short reason code only, deleted after 90 days.</li>
      <li>Newsletter: until you unsubscribe. Kit may keep a record that you unsubscribed, so you aren't emailed again.</li>
      <li>Event and shop listings: while they're useful on the site.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can ask us to delete your information sooner. We'll do it within 30 days.</p>

    <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
    <p>Canada's privacy law for businesses, the Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA), applies to The Celtic Coo, along with Alberta's Personal Information Protection Act (PIPA) where it applies. You can ask to see the personal information we hold about you, have it corrected, or have it deleted.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, or want to see, correct or delete your information? Email <a href="mailto:privacy@celticcoo.ca?subject=Privacy">privacy@celticcoo.ca</a> with "Privacy" in the subject, or write to The Celtic Coo, {MAILING_ADDRESS}. The site owner is responsible for privacy and reads every request. We'll reply within 30 days. If you're not happy with our answer, you can contact the <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada</a> or <a href="https://oipc.ab.ca/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Alberta's Office of the Information and Privacy Commissioner</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we change how we handle information, we'll update this page and the effective date above.</p>
    <p class="muted">See also our <a href={u('terms/')}>Terms of Use</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
